// Type-checking for the TEST tree. `tsconfig.json` includes only `src/**/*`, so
// until this file existed `tsc --noEmit` never looked at a single one of the 571
// files under `tests/` — vitest runs them through esbuild, which STRIPS types
// without checking them. A test could pass a wrong-shaped object to the function
// it is pinning and stay green; measured on 2026-09-02, 201 real type errors were
// sitting in the tree unseen.
//
// WHY A SEPARATE FILE rather than widening `include` in tsconfig.json: that one
// also drives the BUILD (`outDir: dist`, `rootDir: src`). Adding tests to it would
// compile them into the shipped app.
//
// Three compiler options differ from the base and each is load-bearing:
//   * moduleResolution "bundler" / module "esnext" — vitest resolves through Vite,
//     so tests import packages whose types live behind an "exports" map. Under the
//     base's classic "node" resolution, `vite` and `@vitejs/plugin-react` alone
//     produced 12 phantom "cannot find module" errors.
//   * allowJs + checkJs:false — several suites import the untyped
//     `test-engine/*.mjs` orchestrator directly. Without allowJs that is 57
//     implicit-any errors about files this project does not typecheck anyway.
//   * lib DOM.Iterable — `for (const el of document.querySelectorAll(...))` is
//     everywhere in the .tsx suites and is not in the base's lib list.
//
// THE EXCLUDE LIST WAS TECHNICAL DEBT, and it is paid (2026-10-12, close-session friction
// proposal 19): the last 47 files and their 203 errors were fixed — a required prop added to a
// shared card had broken a skipped test only at run time. Every test file is checked now; do not
// add one back to `exclude` — fix its types instead.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "types": ["node", "vitest/globals"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "tests/**/*", "vitest.config.ts", "vite.config.ts"],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist"
  ]
}
